Mindloom patch 0003: take the master key from Mindloom on an inherited descriptor.

Upstream stores its 32-byte master key in the login Keychain through /usr/bin/security, which any
program running as the owner can read without a prompt, and with it decrypt the saved login.
With TMEET_MASTER_KEY_FD set, tmeet reads the key (base64 or 32 raw bytes) from that descriptor,
closes it, clears the variable, and never reads or writes the system Keychain; a missing or
malformed key is an error, with no fallback. Mindloom keeps the key in its own Keychain item.
Without the variable tmeet behaves as upstream.
Regression test: internal/core/keychain/keychain_fd_darwin_test.go.

